{"name":"Sweet Scent","hex":"#c7b7d0","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of sugars.","Retaining a portion of sugar."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Used as a positive response to good news or information."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet"},{"term":"scent","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A distinctive smell.","A smell left by an animal that may be used for tracing."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To detect the scent of; to discern by the sense of smell.","To inhale in order to detect the scent of (something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scent"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pluchea odorata","blocks":[{"text":"Pluchea odorata is a species of flowering plant in the family Asteraceae. Common names include sweetscent, saltmarsh fleabane and shrubby camphorweed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Plucheaodorata.jpg/330px-Plucheaodorata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pluchea_odorata"},{"title":"Odor","blocks":[{"text":"An odor or odour is a smell or a scent caused by one or more volatilized chemical compounds generally found in low concentrations that humans and many animals can perceive via their olfactory system. While smell can refer to pleasant and unpleasant odors, the terms scent, aroma, and fragrance are usually reserved for pleasant-smelling odors and are frequently used in the food and cosmetic industry to describe floral scents or to refer to perfumes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Jan_Brueghel_d._O._-_Allegorie_van_de_geur.jpg/330px-Jan_Brueghel_d._O._-_Allegorie_van_de_geur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Odor"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/